Description:
The Pros - Great location; close to everything; good size rooms; clean; no sign of bed bugs; good exercise room; 
The Cons - The worst and most uncomfortable bed we have ever slept on in a hotel; even lousier pillows; sofa bed (opened it to seek possible relief from the lousy bed) is an absolute joke - don't waste your time booking a room with a sofa bed if you have kids; unfriendly staff; no wi-fi in the rooms and if you want it they charge $--.-- - day - rip off!; free wi-fi in lobby is awful; room decor looks circa ----'s; -- elevators in the hotel yet we found ourselves constantly waiting for elevators especially during busy parts of the day; if you want to go to the restaurant on the top floor just to grab a view of Times Square there is a one drink minimum otherwise they won't let you up there; $--.-- + tax for a phone call; 
For a Marriott Hotel at this price ... sorry folks average at best! Stayed at the Doubletree Suites directly across the street last year and it is a far better hotel. There is a reason why the Doubletree is ranked so much higher than the Marquis by Trip Advisor travellers... its simply a better hotel for the same money. Also, it didn't bother us, but if you don't like crowds, this is not the place for you. This is a busy hotel.

I've been going to Chicago on business for about a year, and I always try to stay at the Renaissance in Chicago downtown with budget permitting. I have a frequent guess status which is a plus. But the things that I like about it over the sister hotels and even the Starwood hotels in the same area are:
-) very good pool and workout area that was free (Starwood charges a fee);
-) great, clean, updated, modern rooms;
-) staff was always friendly;
-) lobby was beautiful;
-) food at club lounge is great; and
-) free shoe shine service.
The Renaissance is my favorite hotel in Chicago.

Pros: Very friendly staff
Cons: -. room was hot and thermostat was ineffective in making it cooler;
-. In room coffee maker had brown slime in the water intake container - even after I cleaned it the water that I ran through the machine came out discolored. I have never seen this before and hope to never see this again. ps., I didn't drink the coffee.
